-- Settings columns (docs/plans/settings-columns-plan.md, v44 gap items 31, 33 and 36, FR-55; pre-approved by the Project manager under Milin's delegation, with this migration). On user_settings, which is owner-only with row level security already: message_requests, "Allow message requests from people who aren't connections" (on by default, so nobody's inbox changes); open_to_work_in, Remote or listed cities, at most 6; usually_free, weekday picker hours as "mon 17:00", at most 40. On applications, open_to_work_in as it was when the person sent that Express apply application. No new table or foreign key, so no new index; both tables go with the account (on delete cascade). None of these is logged or shown on a profile. Expand only: four columns with defaults and three checks.
